    M_IPLR          171/171   TOTAL ESCAPE predicted.
        The IPL arm has TWO function-statics named `w', dev_pcc2.c:629 (write branch) and
        :634 (READ branch, the "IPL == 0 on read" latch).  The restated enumeration names
        ONE ("IPL reads the function-static `w' (its #119 print latch): `ipl wset'").
        Licensed three-part composite, exactly the form the round used for M_IPL_W:
          (1) `static int w_r = 0;' hoisted to DEVICE_ACCESS scope        (inert: a decl move)
          (2) the :634 block static deleted and its two uses renamed w_r  (inert: a rename)
          (3) `&& !w_r' appended to the IPL width guard                   (the live edit)
        WARRANT for the escape: the read latch is set only by a MEM_READ at 0x3e while
        reg[IPL]==0 (the init state).  Sessions that READ IPL -- `hrd ipl'/`hrd ipl lv'/
        `hrd ipl nod', `hrd ipl noro', `brd ipl noro' -- never wide-write IPL.  Sessions
        that WIDE-WRITE IPL -- `ipl noig2/4/8', `ipl wset', `hwr ipl noig', `hwr ipl'/
        `hwr ipl dcl', `latch all', `latch all w', `latch all d', `latch all one' -- never
        read IPL.  No session does both, so w_r is 0 at every decision point.

    M_WARNX         171/171   TOTAL ESCAPE predicted.
        `&& !(d->warned & (1u << PCC2_W_MASK_LEN))' appended to the GENCTL width guard --
        the pass-5 canonical `&& !(d->warned & (1u << bit))' form with ONE TOKEN changed,
        the enum member (the ALIAS slip, which this file's own history has: the MASK arm's
        comment was copy-pasted from IPL and corrected THIS pass).
        WARRANT: `rb2 *' holds each arm's OWN latch bit; nothing holds ANOTHER block's bit
        set at this arm's wide write.  GENCTL is offset 0x02 and is written FIRST in
        BLOCKS12, so in `latch all'/`latch all w'/`latch all d'/`latch all one' MASK's bit
        is still clear when GENCTL is written.  `latch aba' sets VECBASE's bit, not MASK's.
        Every other GENCTL wide-write session (rb genctl, rb genctl dcl, rb vecbase,
        rb genctl lo, rb2 genctl, rb4/rb8 genctl, hwr genctl, latch same, latch two)
        touches MASK not at all.  So the conjunct is TRUE at every GENCTL decision point.

